  message: "PR #291 (selfh/dev 0a73f6beae) delivered the two CORE pieces, closing the systemic gap that let WI-guhas/WI-falum hide: (1) per-(validator_class, severity) shrink-only ratchet dimension on the 4 fixture substrates — kills signed cancellation (a regression in any warning class trips independently, not absorbed by the lumped total); (2) the full-suite-only self-tree-validation gate that DID NOT previously exist — full-suite.yml job -> scripts/check-self-tree-validation -> hypergumbo_core.validation_ratchet.matrix_breaches — runs 'hypergumbo run .' and ratchets the per-cell matrix vs .ci/self-tree-validation-baselines.json (id_format|warning:3012 = the INV-kurup :unresolved cohort, ratchets down when WI-jopil lands; else 0). Logic unit-tested (test_validation_ratchet.py 100%); gate verified end-to-end locally (matrix {id_format|warning:3012} within baseline -> exit 0; tightened baseline 3000 -> breach -> exit 1). RESIDUAL (now todo_soft, hardening not hole): the _WIRED_CHECKS per-check enforcement-field meta-rule (each wired check declares error-floor|ratchet-dimension|advisory + a test asserting no check claims 'enforced' while total-count-only) and per-PR fixture coverage so every check fires on >=1 substrate."  # 289c
